      "file": "items/thm-yangian-evaluation-module-well-defined.md",
      "item_id": "thm-yangian-evaluation-module-well-defined",
      "status": "repair",
      "strategy": "direct",
      "proposed_proof": "**Given:** The RTT Yangian of [[def-yangian-gl-n-rtt-presentation]], a $\\mathfrak{gl}_N$-module $W$, its action $\\rho$, and a spectral shift $a\\in\\mathbb C$.\n\n[F1] [[def-yangian-gl-n-rtt-presentation]]: $R_N(x)=xI+iP_N$, and the defining relation is $R_{12}(u-v)T_1(u)T_2(v)=T_2(v)T_1(u)R_{12}(u-v)$.\n\n[F2] [[def-yangian-evaluation-module]]: the proposed generator action is $t_{ij}(u)=\\delta_{ij}I_W-i\\rho(E_{ij})/(u-a)$, and the dual-natural action is $E_{ij}f^k=-\\delta_{ik}f^j$.\n\n[F3] [[def-matrix-units]]: $E_{ij}$ is the matrix with entries $(E_{ij})_{rs}=\\delta_{ri}\\delta_{sj}$.\n\n[F4] [[lem-yangian-rtt-component-commutator-form]]: $x[t_{ij}(u),t_{kl}(v)]=i(t_{kj}(v)t_{il}(u)-t_{kj}(u)t_{il}(v))$ for $x=u-v$ is equivalent to the matrix RTT relation.\n\n\n\n1.1 Let $e_1,\\ldots,e_N$ be the standard column basis. By [F3], $E_{ij}e_s=\\delta_{js}e_i$, so $E_{ij}E_{kl}e_s=\\delta_{jk}\\delta_{ls}e_i=(\\delta_{jk}E_{il})e_s$ for every $s$. Hence $E_{ij}E_{kl}=\\delta_{jk}E_{il}$ and $[E_{ij},E_{kl}]=\\delta_{jk}E_{il}-\\delta_{li}E_{kj}$. On a dual basis vector $f^s$, the explicit commutator is $[\\rho^\\vee(E_{ij}),\\rho^\\vee(E_{kl})]f^s=\\delta_{ks}\\delta_{il}f^j-\\delta_{is}\\delta_{jk}f^l$. The right side is also $\\rho^\\vee(\\delta_{jk}E_{il}-\\delta_{li}E_{kj})f^s$, by the same formula. Thus the dual-natural operators satisfy the matrix-unit bracket and form a $\\mathfrak{gl}_N$-representation. [given, F2, F3, algebra]\n\n2.1 Put $x=u-v$, $U=u-a$, and $V=v-a$. By [F4], the required component identity is the RTT relation to check. Under [F2], its left side is $-x(\\delta_{jk}\\rho(E_{il})-\\delta_{li}\\rho(E_{kj}))/(UV)$ by the bracket relation. In the parenthesized difference on the right, the quadratic terms cancel because both are $(-i)^2\\rho(E_{kj})\\rho(E_{il})/(UV)$. Its linear terms are $-i\\delta_{kj}\\rho(E_{il})(U^{-1}-V^{-1})-i\\delta_{il}\\rho(E_{kj})(V^{-1}-U^{-1})=ix(\\delta_{jk}\\rho(E_{il})-\\delta_{li}\\rho(E_{kj}))/(UV)$, since $V-U=-x$. Multiplication by the outer factor $i$ therefore gives the same left side. Thus every component RTT relation holds. [given, F2, F4, step 1.1, algebra]\n\n3.1 The component relations are exactly the coefficients of the matrix relation [F1]. Thus the images of every defining relation vanish, so the assignment on the free generators factors through the RTT quotient and defines the representation $W(a)$. For $W=V_N^\\vee$, its auxiliary matrix is $I+iP_N/(u-a)$ by the explicit sum $\\sum_{i,j}E_{ij}\\otimes E_{ji}=P_N$; multiplying by $u-a$ gives $R_N(u-a)$. [given, F1, F2, step 1.1, step 2.1, algebra] ∎"
    },
